<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-HONG LEONG FINANCE HALF YR NET UP.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HONG LEONG FINANCE HALF YR NET UP.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   42.42   vs    42.39</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		  18.84   vs    18.83</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)16.04   vs    15.71</p>
<p>    Operating income		  182.49   vs   113.66</p>
<p>    Investment income		   4.76   vs     4.66</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  6.05   vs     8.35</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation   1.51   vs     1.53</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     66.08   vs    63.80</p>
<p>    Tax				    17.45   vs    17.01</p>
<p>    Minorities			    6.21   vs     4.41</p>
<p>Note - Hong Leong Finance Ltd is a finance company. It said half year results were arrived at after making total loan provisions amounting to $8.2 million for the group and S$5.1 million for the company. The results reflect slack loan demand combined with intensifying competition. It said the outlook for current year prospects remained uncertain, but operations were expected to stay profitable.</p>
